 being applied.\n\nPass the explorer a self-contained question with explicit scope\n(\"all of `docs/site/guide/`\", \"the `lib/parsers/` module\"). It does\nnot see your conversation. Be clear about the level of detail\nexpected.\n\n## Style\n\nNever start a response by calling the user's question or idea good,\ngreat, fascinating, profound, excellent, or perfect. Skip flattery\nand respond directly. Don't pad replies with \"happy to help\",\n\"certainly\", or trailing summaries the user can read in the diff.\n\n**Use ASCII diagrams when they clarify.** For control flow, state\nmachines, pipelines, module relationships, or any \"how do the parts\nfit together\" answer, draw a small ASCII diagram in a fenced\n```text block. Boxes, arrows, and trees beat paragraphs for\nstructural explanations:\n\n```text\nparse → SymbolTable.build → preprocess → TypeScriptBuilder → printTs\n```\n\nKeep diagrams small. Skip them where prose or code is clearer —\ndiagrams earn their space by showing **relationships** or **flow**.\n\n## Be proactive\n\nWhen the user asks you to look at, debug, or change a file or some code,\n**delegate to `codeAgent` to do it** — don't ask the user to paste a file\nor describe code a subagent could read. The code agent has `read`, `glob`,\nand `ls` and resolves relative paths against the user's working directory\nautomatically, so a bare filename like `foo.agency` is enough. Only ask\nthe user for information you genuinely cannot obtain through a subagent.\n\n## Answer before action\n\nWhen the user asks a question, asks for an opinion, or asks how to\nplan or approach something, **answer the question first**. Don't\njump straight into delegating to a subagent or making tool calls\nunless the user has clearly asked for an action (\"do X\", \"fix Y\",\n\"build Z\"). If the user is exploring or thinking out loud, think\nwith them — don't sprint to implementation.\n\n## Communicating with the user\n- Make sure the user is following what you're doing. Use the `whatIAmDoing` tool frequently to tell the user what you're doing.\n- Also use the `elapsedTime` tool frequently to check how much time has elapsed since you started the task. If the user gave you a time constraint to work within, make sure you finish the task within that time constraint. For simple tasks, make sure you don't spend too long researching things before giving an answer.\n\n\n  Current date: 2026-07-23\n  Current working directory: /Users/adityabhargava/agency-lang/packages/agency-lang\n  \n  "},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"What are today's top news stories? Please answer quickly"}]},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"toolCalls":[{"id":"toolu_01Y9NDSYrTwQsxNNRSeX351g","name":"whatIAmDoing","arguments":{"message":"Looking up today's top news headlines via web search."}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"Delivered message to user.","name":"whatIAmDoing","tool_call_id":"toolu_01Y9NDSYrTwQsxNNRSeX351g"}],"completion":{"output":null,"toolCalls":[{"id":"toolu_014ezrqd7jgrLt3gimVnWHCB","name":"researchAgent","arguments":{"userMsg":"What are the top news stories today, July 23, 2026? Please give a brief summary of the 5-6 most significant world/national news headlines from today.","agencyTopic":false}}],"usage":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":133,"totalTokens":5621,"cachedInputTokens":5407,"cacheCreationInputTokens":79},"cost":{"inputCost":0.000006,"outputCost":0.001995,"cachedInputCost":0.001622,"cacheCreationInputCost":0.000296,"totalCost":0.003919,"currency":"USD"},"model":"claude-sonnet-5","stopReason":"tool_use","rawStopReason":"tool_use","thinkingBlocks":[{"text":"","signature":""}]},"model":"\"claude-sonnet-5\"","timeTaken":2038.432249999998,"tools":[{"name":"researchAgent","description":"Answer a question that needs reading rather than writing: looking something\n  up, summarizing a document, gathering background, or recalling a stored\n  fact.\n\n  @param userMsg - a message describing what needs to be found out.\n  @param agencyTopic - true when the question is about the Agency language\n    itself (its syntax, types, stdlib, or CLI), which routes to the agent\n    that reads the bundled Agency documentation. Leave it false for every\n    other subject, including questions about other languages.","schema":{"def":{"type":"object","shape":{"userMsg":{"def":{"type":"string"},"type":"string","format":null,"minLength":null,"maxLength":null},"agencyTopic":{"def":{"type":"nullable","innerType":{"def":{"type":"boolean"},"type":"boolean"}},"type":"nullable"}}},"type":"object"}},{"name":"codeAgent","description":"This agent can help with all coding-related tasks,\n  such as reading, writing, or editing code. It can also\n  respond to questions about the Agency language,\n  such as questions related to the Agency syntax or CLI tool.\n\n  @param userMsg - a message describing what help is needed.\n  @param agencyTask - true when the code in question is Agency code, which\n    routes to the agents that know the language. Leave it false for every\n    other language.","schema":{"def":{"type":"object","shape":{"userMsg":{"def":{"type":"string"},"type":"string","format":null,"minLength":null,"maxLength":null},"agencyTask":{"def":{"type":"nullable","innerType":{"def":{"type":"boolean"},"type":"boolean"}},"type":"nullable"}}},"type":"object"}},{"name":"reviewAgent","description":"Review code and report what is wrong with it: errors, risks, and things\n  worth changing.\n\n  @param userMsg - the code to review, or a message describing what to review.\n  @param agencyTask - true when the code is Agency code, which routes to the\n    reviewer that parses and typechecks it. Leave it false for every other\n    language, where that reviewer has nothing useful to say.","schema":{"def":{"type":"object","shape":{"userMsg":{"def":{"type":"string"},"type":"string","format":null,"minLength":null,"maxLength":null},"agencyTask":{"def":{"type":"nullable","innerType":{"def":{"type":"boolean"},"type":"boolean"}},"type":"nullable"}}},"type":"object"}},{"name":"oracleAgent","description":"Ask the oracle — a read-only senior reviewer on a stronger\n  reasoning model — for a second opinion on a hard problem. Call\n  this BEFORE acting when:\n\n  - You're about to execute a non-trivial plan and want it sanity-\n    checked (\"is this a good plan? is there a simpler way?\")\n  - You suspect existing code already solves the problem and want\n    a thorough search (\"is there a helper for X in this repo?\")\n  - You're stuck on a bug after one or two failed attempts\n  - You want a critical review of a diff or design before showing\n    it to the user\n\n  Pass a self-contained question with full context — the oracle\n  starts fresh and does not see your conversation. Include the\n  plan, the relevant file paths, what you've already tried, and\n  the specific question you want answered. The oracle returns a\n  written analysis.\n\n  @param userMsg - the question, with all the context the oracle\n    needs to answer it","schema":{"def":{"type":"object","shape":{"userMsg":{"def":{"type":"string"},"type":"string","format":null,"minLength":null,"maxLength":null}}},"type":"object"}},{"name":"explorerAgent","description":"Ask the explorer — a read-only researcher on a stronger\n  reasoning model — to produce a broad, synthesizing answer about\n  the codebase or the bundled Agency docs.\n\n  Use this when the user asks a question whose answer requires\n  **reading many files and synthesizing**:\n\n  - \"Summarize the Agency docs\"\n  - \"What are the main features of X?\"\n  - \"Give me a tour of module Y\"\n  - \"How does Z work across the codebase?\"\n  - \"Walk me through the compilation pipeline\"\n\n  Do NOT use this for:\n  - Targeted lookups (use `codeAgent` or just `grep`)\n  - Plan critique or bug diagnosis (use `oracleAgent`)\n  - External / web research (use `researchAgent`)\n\n  Pass a self-contained question — the explorer starts fresh and\n  does not see your conversation. Be explicit about