{"format_version":1,"trace_id":"JCdVnnRn7lhXe8HDoU0pv","project_id":"agency-lang","span_id":"rP5E9d1qZ273","parent_span_id":"fPQjDucwJz89","data":{"type":"toolCall","toolName":"web_search_tavily","args":{"query":"Ukraine protests defense minister ousted July 2026","count":5,"topic":"news"},"output":[{"title":"Zelensky ousts popular defense minister, an architect of Ukraine’s drone program - The Washington Post","url":"https://www.washingtonpost.com/world/2026/07/16/zelensky-ousts-popular-defense-minister-an-architect-ukraines-drone-program/","description":"Mykhailo Fedorov's dismissal, part of a rebooting of the government announced Sunday, prompted protests in Kyiv. He was defense minister for barely six months. KYIV — Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky has ousted the country’s popular defense minister, Mykhailo Fedorov, prompting protests in Kyiv over a fear that his removal will jeopardize the war effort just as Ukraine is scoring victories on the front line. Although Zelensky did not announce it, Fedorov and members of the president’s Servant of the People party confirmed the dismissal late Wednesday — part of a rebooting of the government announced Sunday and among the latest signs of top-level turmoil. But he said that the decision was linked in part to his dispute with the head of the Ukrainian armed forces, Oleksandr Syrsky, with whom he disagreed over a number of issues related to the war."},{"title":"Zelensky sacks Ukraine’s military chief following widespread protests - CNN","url":"https://www.cnn.com/2026/07/21/europe/ukraine-military-chief-sacked-intl","description":"# Zelensky sacks Ukraine’s military chief following widespread protests. Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky has replaced Kyiv’s military chief, General Oleksandr Syrskyi, after days of widespread protests against the removal of the country’s popular defense minister, whose ousting revealed an unprecedented public split in the military over its strategy in the war against Russia. Mykhailo Drapatyi, who is the commander of Ukraine’s Joint Forces, will become Ukraine’s new commander-in-chief, Zelensky announced on Tuesday evening. Meanwhile, Zelensky offered Mykhailo Fedorov, whose removal as defense minister sparked this political storm, a “prominent position in government that would allow him to unify the technical component of our state and ensure its development.”. Aged 35 years old, Fedorov carved out a reputation as pioneering innovative approaches to technology and recruitment but clashed with other members of Ukraine’s defense establishment. His six-month tenure as defense minister coincided with Ukraine’s recent success on the battlefield and so his removal, amid disagreements with Syrskyi, caused a backlash against the military chief. *This is a developing story and will be updated.*."},{"title":"Ukrainians protest Zelensky’s ouster of his popular defense minister - Los Angeles Times","url":"https://www.latimes.com/world-nation/story/2026-07-16/ukrainians-protest-zelenskys-ouster-of-his-popular-defense-minister","description":"# Ukrainians protest Zelensky’s ouster of his popular defense minister. * Zelensky shakes up wartime leadership, firing popular 35-year-old defense minister Mykhailo Fedorov, a drone warfare innovator, sparking rare street protests as Russia’s invasion nears four-and-a-half years. KYIV, Ukraine — President Volodymyr Zelensky shook up his wartime government, drawing hundreds of Ukrainians into the streets Thursday to protest the ouster of his youthful defense minister — seen as an innovator of the country’s successful drone technology but who clashed with the traditional military establishment. The personnel overhaul, which included replacing his prime minister, could become a test of Zelensky’s political authority as Ukraine’s fight against Russia’s full-scale invasion approaches 4½ years. The moves threw Ukraine’s military leadership into an unwelcome crisis just as its actions against Russia were starting to bear fruit and came against a backdrop of Moscow’s unrelenting aerial attacks. Zelensky cited friction between outgoing Defense Minister Mykhailo Fedorov and Gen. Oleksandr Syrskyi, the commander of Ukraine’s armed forces."},{"title":"What to know about Ukraine's military shakeup - NPR","url":"https://www.npr.org/2026/07/22/g-s1-134813/ukraine-military-shakeup-zelenskyy","description":"**What to know about Ukraine's military shakeup** **After a week of nationwide protests over the direction of Ukraine's military strategy in the ongoing war with Russia, the Ukrainian military has a new commander, Mykhailo Drapatyi. # What to know about Ukraine's military shakeup. Protests erupted in Kyiv on Friday as President Volodymyr Zelenskyy dismissed Mykhailo Fedorov as Ukraine's defense minister. KYIV — After a week of nationwide protests over the direction of Ukraine's military strategy in the ongoing war with Russia, the Ukrainian military has a new armed forces commander, Mykhailo Drapatyi. In this photo provided by the Ukrainian Presidential Press Office, new commander-in-chief of Ukraine's Armed Forces Mykhailo Drapatyi looks on during his meeting with Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy in Kyiv, Ukraine, Monday, July 20, 2026. He is also the face of a younger, post-Soviet generation of military leaders in Ukraine who are adapting more quickly to a tech-focused approach to the battlefield."},{"title":"Protests continue in Ukraine over defense minister's firing - NPR","url":"https://www.npr.org/2026/07/20/nx-s1-5899777/protests-continue-in-ukraine-over-defense-ministers-firing","description":"* Keyboard shortcuts for audio player. **Protests continue in Ukraine over defense minister's firing** **Protests over President Volodymyr Zelenskyy's dismissal of the country's defense minister coincide with a fresh wave of Russian strikes across Ukraine.**. ### Europe. # Protests continue in Ukraine over defense minister's firing. * **`<iframe src=\"https://www.npr.org/player/embed/nx-s1-5899777/nx-s1-9854967\" width=\"100%\" height=\"290\" frameborder=\"0\" scrolling=\"no\" title=\"NPR embedded audio player\">`**. Protests over President Volodymyr Zelenskyy's dismissal of the country's defense minister coincide with a fresh wave of Russian strikes across Ukraine."}],"model":"\"claude-sonnet-5\"","timeTaken":662.2791670000006,"threadId":"0","timestamp":"2026-07-23T13:55:23.739Z"}}
{"format_version":1,"trace_id":"JCdVnnRn7lhXe8HDoU0pv","project_id":"agency-lang","span_id":"D3UAw-6xHqEs","parent_span_id":"fPQjDucwJz89","data":{"type":"toolCall","toolName":"web_search_tavily","args":{"query":"US Iran strikes today July 23 2026","count":6,"topic":"news"},"output":[{"title":"U.S. and Iranian attacks continue as tensions mount on a key waterway in the Red Sea - Jefferson Public Radio","url":"https://www.ijpr.org/npr-news/2026-07-22/u-s-and-iranian-attacks-continue-as-tensions-mount-on-a-key-waterway-in-the-red-sea","description":"# U.S. and Iranian attacks continue as tensions mount on a key waterway in the Red Sea. Published July 22, 2026 at 3:46 AM PDT. The U.S. military launched more airstrikes on Iran early Wednesday as Iran hit back against U.S. military targets in the Gulf and Jordan. It said the attacks were aimed at degrading Iran's control over the Strait of Hormuz – a vital shipping channel. The Shia Muslim Houthis are backed by Iran and a key part of Iran's \"axis of resistance,\" which has joined in attacks on U.S. and Israeli targets. Iran said Wednesday it again targeted an air base in eastern Jordan where three U.S. military personnel were killed in an attack last week. Iran blames the U.S. for the missile strike on the first day of the U.S.-Israeli war on Iran and says it killed at least 156 people, including 120 children. Iran says 168 students and teachers were killed in a U.S. missile strike on the school in southern Iran on Feb. 28."},{"title":"U.S. and Iranian attacks continue as tensions mount on a key waterway in the Red Sea - Northern Public Radio","url":"https://www.northernpublicradio.org/2026-07-22/u-s-and-iranian-attacks-continue-as-tensions-mount-on-a-key-waterway-in-the-red-sea","description":"# U.S. and Iranian attacks continue as tensions mount on a key waterway in the Red Sea. Published July 22, 2026 at 5:46 AM CDT. The U.S. military launched more airstrikes on Iran early Wednesday as Iran hit back against U.S. military targets in the Gulf and Jordan. It said the attacks were aimed at degrading Iran's control over the Strait of Hormuz – a vital shipping channel. Iranian state media reported explosions in seven Iranian provinces and said attacks included a strike on an electrical installation close to a nuclear power plant in Bushehr province. The Shia Muslim Houthis are backed by Iran and a key part of Iran's \"axis of resistance,\" which has joined in attacks on U.S. and Israeli targets. Iran said Wednesday it again targeted an air base in eastern Jordan where three U.S. military personnel were killed in an attack last week."},{"title":"US launches strikes against Iran for ninth consecutive night, sirens sound in Kuwait, Bahrain - The Jerusalem Post","url":"https://www.jpost.com/middle-east/iran-news/article-903012","description":"# US launches strikes against Iran for ninth consecutive night, sirens sound in Kuwait, Bahrain. ## \"The strikes will continue degrading Iranian military capabilities used to attack commercial vessels and civilian mariners transiting the Strait of Hormuz,\" CENTCOM wrote. A munition is launched from a U.S. warship at an unknown location, during what U.S. Central Command (CENTCOM) says are strikes on Iran, in this screen grab taken from a handout video released on July 18, 2026. (photo credit: US CENTRAL COMMAND/HANDOUT VIA REUTERS). The United States launched a new wave of strikes against Iran early Monday morning, US Central Command (CENTCOM) stated in a post to X/Twitter. This marks the ninth consecutive night of US strikes against Iran. Iran has been retaliating by targeting US bases and other infrastructure in neighboring countries. Earlier on Sunday night, the Kuwait military announced it was intercepting multiple hostile drones. Additionally, sirens were sounded in Kuwait. *This is a developing story.*."},{"title":"US military says it completed latest strikes on Iran, marking 6th consecutive night of attacks - Reuters","url":"https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/us-military-says-it-completed-latest-strikes-iran-marking-6th-consecutive-night-2026-07-17/","description":"## Browse World. Smoke rises from an explosion at an unknown location, during what U.S. Central Command (CENTCOM) says are strikes on Iran, in this screen grab taken from a handout video released on July 15, 2026. U.S. Central Command/Handout via REUTERS Purchase Licensing Rights, opens new tab. WASHINGTON, July 16 (Reuters) - The U.S. military said late on Thursday it completed its latest wave of strikes on Iran that were carried out at ​President Donald Trump's direction and marked a sixth consecutive night of American strikes. The Reuters Iran Briefing newsletter keeps you informed with the latest developments and analysis of the Iran war. *   Iranian news outlets also reported U.S. strikes late on ​Thursday on three bridges and the train station in coastal Bandar Khamir and a U.S. missile attack on Iranshahr Airport in southeastern Iran. *   The Iran war began when the U.S. and Israel attacked Iran on February 28 and Iran responded with its own strikes on Israel and Gulf states that ⁠host ​U.S. bases. *   About Reuters, opens new tab."},{"title":"Iran claims US warplanes strike in southern Iran - The Jerusalem Post","url":"https://www.jpost.com/middle-east/iran-news/article-902943","description":"# US warplanes strike in southern Iran, CENTCOM wraps up eighth round of strikes - report. ## This comes after CENTCOM said that it had completed its eighth consecutive night of strikes against Iran overnight on Saturday. Smoke rises from an explosion at an unknown location, during what U.S. Central Command (CENTCOM) says are strikes on Iran, in this screen grab taken from a handout video released on July 18, 2026. (photo credit: U.S. Central Command/Handout via REUTERS). US warplanes reportedly struck near the city of Shadagan in southern Iran on Sunday, state TV reported. Earlier on Sunday, US Central Command (CENTCOM) said that it had completed its eighth consecutive night of strikes against Iran and hit Iranian military coastal surveillance and air defense facilities. It also targeted the Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps forces that launched attacks against US service members in Jordan on July 17. *This is a developing story.*."},{"title":"US strikes Iran for 9th night, confirms American servicemember killed in Iraq - The Times of Israel","url":"https://www.timesofisrael.com/us-strikes-iran-for-9th-night-confirms-american-servicemember-killed-in-iraq/","description":"## Explosions reported in several Iranian cities as IRGC claims it hit oil tankers trying to cross Hormuz, struck assets in Kuwait; Iran said to suspect US planning ground operation. Video footage shared by US Central Command on July 19, 2026, shows forces launching a ninth consecutive evening of strikes against Iran. US forces struck Iran for a ninth consecutive day on Monday as the number of confirmed American military deaths in the renewed fighting rose to three, and concerns grew over shipping through the Strait of Hormuz, which the Trump administration accused the Islamic Republic of seeking to control “as leverage against the world.”. Announcing the latest casualties in the war, the US military said on Sunday that a servicemember was killed on Saturday in northern Iraq, where the US has military bases, “during a controlled detonation” of a downed Iranian attack drone."}],"model":"\"claude-sonnet-5\"","timeTaken":945.2434580000045,"threadId":"0","timestamp":"2026-07-23T13:55:24.021Z"}}
