scription":"Test Your News I.Q. 2026 Elections Election Results Election calendar White House Congress Supreme Court The latest AP-NORC polls. 2026 Elections Election Results Election calendar White House Congress Supreme Court The latest AP-NORC polls. President Donald Trump used a primetime address to the nation Thursday to elevate his yearslong push to raise doubts about the legitimacy of U.S. elections and dispute his 2020 loss in an appeal for more restrictive voting laws ahead of the midterms. “Starting during the 2020 election cycle, the People’s Republic of China carried out what is believed to be the largest compromise of election data in history, resulting in China’s illicit acquisition of 220 million U.S. voter files,” Trump said Thursday night. In his remarks, Trump touted the release of a new Department of Homeland Security investigation, based on state voter rolls and public records, that he said had identified approximately 278,000 noncitizens registered to vote in federal elections."},{"title":"Newly declassified documents offer scant evidence for Trump’s election claims - NBC News","url":"https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/elections/newly-declassified-documents-scant-evidence-trump-election-claims-rcna587971","description":"IE 11 is not supported. For an optimal experience visit our site on another browser. # Newly declassified documents offer scant evidence for Trump’s election claims. The president attempted to paint a picture of a vulnerable election system, but the documents don’t fully back up his allegations. President Donald Trump delivered an address to the nation from the East Room of the White House on July 16, 2026.Saul Loeb / Pool / AFP via Getty Images. Add NBC News to Google. President Donald Trump’s sweeping claims of foreign interference in elections and the vulnerability of voting to attacks aren’t fully backed up by the newly declassified files released by his administration. We are getting your experience ready."}],"name":"web_search_tavily","tool_call_id":"toolu_0174NDVgajdfHMu65f5cBTrR"},{"role":"tool","content":[{"title":"Map: 7.3-Magnitude Earthquake Hits Off Mexico's Coast - The New York Times","url":"https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2026/07/17/world/earthquake-mexico-guatemala.html","description":"# Map: 7.3-Magnitude Earthquake Hits Off Mexico's Coast. Note: Map shows the area with a shake intensity of 3 or greater, which U.S.G.S. defines as “weak,” though the earthquake may be felt outside the areas shown. All times on the map are Mexico Central time. A major, 7.3-magnitude earthquake struck in the North Pacific Ocean on Friday, according to the United States Geological Survey. The temblor happened at 8:48 a.m. Mexico Central time about 30 miles southwest of Aquiles Serdán, Mexico, data from the agency shows. U.S.G.S. data earlier reported that the magnitude was 7.4. As seismologists review available data, they may revise the earthquake’s reported magnitude. Additional information collected about the earthquake may also prompt U.S.G.S. scientists to update the shake-severity map. ## Quakes and aftershocks within 100 miles. Shake data is as of Friday, July 17 at 9:08 a.m. Mexico Central time. Aftershocks data is as of Friday, July 17 at 10:17 a.m. Mexico Central time."},{"title":"Mexico Earthquake: Map Shows Where 7.3 Magnitude Tremor Hit Near Puerto Madero - Newsweek","url":"https://www.newsweek.com/mexico-earthquake-puerto-madero-usgs-map-magnitude-12211196","description":"# Mexico Earthquake: Map Shows Where 7.3 Magnitude Tremor Hit Coastline. A powerful magnitude 7.3 earthquake struck off the southern coast of Mexico early Friday morning, rattling the region and triggering immediate infrastructure reviews by emergency officials. The U.S. Geological Survey (USGS) said the quake struck near the Pacific coast of Chiapas state. The tremor occurred at a shallow depth, a factor that typically amplifies the intensity of shaking and expands the area where it can be felt. ## 7.3 Magnitude Earthquake in Mexico Today: Where Was the Epicenter? Preliminary data from the USGS placed the epicenter approximately 48 kilometers (30 miles) southwest of Aquiles Serdán, a coastal community in Chiapas, and not far from the port town of Puerto Madero near the Guatemala border. A map from the USGS shows where the powerful quake struck in southern Mexico on Friday. *Contact Newsweek editors for this story: Kate Nalepinski and Anthony Murray.*."},{"title":"Magnitude 7.3 quake hits Mexican coast near Guatemala, triggering tsunami alert","url":"https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260717-magnitude-7-3-quake-hits-mexican-coast-near-guatemala-triggering-tsunami-alert","description":"*   By clicking \"Accept\", you consent to the use of cookies or similar technologies by France Médias Monde and its partners. A powerful earthquake struck the southern Mexican Pacific coast on Friday, prompting residents to evacuate buildings in neighbouring Guatemala and El Salvador – and triggering an alert from the US Tsunami Warning System. Image 2: People evacuate a building after a powerful 7.4-magnitude earthquake struck off the coast of Mexico's southern state of Chiapas, triggering a tsunami warning and shaking buildings in neighboring Guate. People evacuate a building in San Salvador on July 17, 2026, after a powerful 7.4-magnitude earthquake struck off the coast of Mexico's southern state of Chiapas, triggering a tsunami warning and shaking buildings in neighbouring Guatemala and El Salvador. A powerful magnitude 7.3earthquakestruck near the coast of Mexico's southernmost state of Chiapas on Friday, triggering a tsunami warning and shaking buildings in neighbouring Guatemala and El Salvador."},{"title":"7.3 magnitude earthquake strikes Mexico and Guatemala coasts ...","url":"https://www.euronews.com/2026/07/17/magnitude-73-earthquake-strikes-mexico-and-guatemala-coasts-tsunami-alert-issued","description":"In each episode, two political heavyweights from across the EU face off to propose a diversity of opinions and spark conversations around the most important issues of EU affairs and the wider European political life. ## A 7.3 magnitude earthquake shook the coasts of Mexico and Guatemala on Friday, its epicentre off Chiapas at about 15 km deep, triggering a tsunami alert for dangerous waves within a 300 km radius. A 7.3-magnitude earthquake struck the coast of the Mexican state of Chiapas on Friday, near the border with Guatemala, triggering a tsunami alert for several areas of the Pacific. The tremor was felt most strongly in the Mexican states of Chiapas and Oaxaca, as well as in Guatemala and El Salvador, according to journalists on the ground. In a post on X, Mexican President Claudia Sheinbaum said she had spoken with the governors of Chiapas and Tabasco and that, so far, no damage had been reported in either state."},{"title":"Major magnitude 7.3 earthquake reported off coast of Mexico in Pacific Ring of Fire | Fox Weather","url":"https://www.foxweather.com/extreme-weather/tsunami-threat-issued-mexico-guatemala-after-major-magnitude-7-3-earthquake","description":"The FOX Weather App Learn More. Fox Weather App on an iPhone, Fox Weather logo overlapping. # Tsunami threat issued for Mexico, Guatemala after magnitude 7.3 earthquake along the Pacific Ring of Fire. ## A tsunami threat was issued for Mexico and Guatemala within 186 miles of the earthquake's epicenter. ## Magnitude 7.3 earthquake strikes off the coast of western Mexico. A major earthquake struck off the coast of Mexico, near the Guatemala border on Friday morning, causing a tsunami threat to be issued for the coasts of both countries. The earthquake happened at 7:48 a.m. Pacific time, and was originally reported as a magnitude 7.4 before being recalculated as a magnitude 7.3. **UNDERSTANDING THE PACIFIC RING OF FIRE: WHERE EARTHQUAKES AND VOLCANOES MEET**. **HOW TO WATCH FOX WEATHER**. This is the latest in a string of large earthquakes in the Pacific Ring of Fire. The Ring of Fire is a 25,000-mile belt of volcanoes and earthquake zones surrounding much of the Pacific Ocean."}],"name":"web_search_tavily","tool_call_id":"toolu_014MVsoDUvx1xR5WczpqmHnu"}],"completion":{"output":null,"toolCalls":[{"id":"toolu_01JTB3H1eYyWwTd7T5FnLaQk","name":"web_search_tavily","arguments":{"query":"Iran war news","count":6,"topic":"news","searchDepth":"advanced"}},{"id":"toolu_019xz9y8vDETqkHttp2mWvu5","name":"web_search_tavily","arguments":{"query":"breaking news","count":8,"topic":"news"}}],"usage":{"inputTokens":2120,"outputTokens":436,"totalTokens":36774,"cachedInputTokens":29215,"cacheCreationInputTokens":5003},"cost":{"inputCost":0.00636,"outputCost":0.00654,"cachedInputCost":0.008765,"cacheCreationInputCost":0.018761,"totalCost":0.040426,"currency":"USD"},"model":"claude-sonnet-5","stopReason":"tool_use","rawStopReason":"tool_use","thinkingBlocks":[{"text":"","signature":""}]},"model":"\"claude-sonnet-5\"","timeTaken":5639.589791999999,"tools":[{"name":"fetch","description":"Fetch a URL and return the response as text.\n\n  @param baseUrl - The base URL to fetch\n  @param path - Optional path appended to baseUrl\n  @param headers - Custom request headers\n  @param allowedDomains - Restrict fetches to these domains (empty allows all)\n  @param method - The HTTP method\n  @param body - Request body: a string is sent as-is, a non-string is sent as JSON","schema":{"def":{"type":"object","shape":{"baseUrl":{"def":{"type":"string"},"type":"string","format":null,"minLength":null,"maxLength":null},"path":{"def":{"type":"nullable","innerType":{"def":{"type":"string"},"type":"string","format":null,"minLength":null,"maxLength":null}},"type":"nullable"},"headers":{"def":{"type":"nullable","innerType":{"def":{"type":"record","keyType":{"def":{"type":"string"},"type":"string","format":null,"minLength":null,"maxLength":null},"valueType":{"def":{"type":"any"},"type":"any"}},"type":"record","keyType":{"def":{"type":"string"},"type":"string","format":null,"minLen