y, Chongqing, China July 17, 2026. BEIJING, July 17 (Reuters) - Eight people were killed ​and 34 others are still missing after a landslide in a ‌county in the southwestern Chinese city of Chongqing on Friday, local government officials told a press conference. In a late Friday directive, President Xi Jinping ordered search and ​rescue operations to be carried out for the missing and called ​for an investigation into the cause of the landslide. *   About Reuters, opens new tab. *   Media Center, opens new tab."},{"title":"Landslide in southwest China traps people, rescue efforts underway - AP News","url":"https://apnews.com/article/china-landslide-chongqing-buildings-127e504babcf9d70773e4ec67af34952","description":"Test Your News I.Q. 2026 Elections Election Results Election calendar White House Congress Supreme Court The latest AP-NORC polls. 2026 Elections Election Results Election calendar White House Congress Supreme Court The latest AP-NORC polls. Founded in 1846, AP today remains the most trusted source of fast, accurate, unbiased news in all formats and the essential provider of the technology and services vital to the news business. In this photo released by Xinhua News Agency, rescuers conduct search and rescue operation on the site of the landslide in Pengshui County in southwestern China’s Chongqing on Friday, July 17, 2026. In this photo taken and provided by Mimama, smoke rise as resident buildings toppled by rocks and muds following a landslide in Pengshui County in southwestern China’s Chongqing on Friday, July 17, 2026. This photo taken and provided by Mimama shows firefighters arrive to the landslide scene in Pengshui County in southwestern China’s Chongqing on Friday, July 17, 2026."}],"name":"web_search_tavily","tool_call_id":"toolu_0181zTz6i4pxSfDLLod2RfiW"},{"role":"tool","content":[{"title":"Spain, scoring late, tops Argentina, 1-0, to win 2026 World Cup - The Washington Post","url":"https://www.washingtonpost.com/sports/2026/07/19/spain-scoring-late-tops-argentina-1-0-win-2026-world-cup/","description":"# Spain, scoring late, tops Argentina, 1-0, to win 2026 World Cup. A tournament that began as a grand experiment across three countries ended with a finish worthy of all its sprawl: Spain beating Argentina, 1-0, in extra time. Ferran Torres, Spain’s flashy 26-year-old forward, put the ball high into the net in the 106th minute of Sunday’s World Cup final, breaking a scoreless tie and sending all of Spain into delirium. And with that, a tournament that began as a grand experiment across three countries ended with a finish worthy of all its sprawl: Spain beating Argentina, 1*-*0, in extra time to win its first World Cup title since 2010 and deny Lionel Messi one more implausible addition to his legend. To get here, Spain masterfully navigated the biggest, most complicated World Cup the sport has seen, bouncing across a continent, slaying the game’s giants and adding both theatrics and closure to a tournament that was never short on drama."},{"title":"2026 World Cup: Spain 1-0 Argentina (AET): Ferran Torres' extra-time winner secures Spain's second title - Sky Sports","url":"https://www.skysports.com/football/news/12098/13564318/2026-world-cup-spain-1-0-argentina-aet-ferran-torres-extra-time-winner-secures-spains-second-title","description":"# 2026 World Cup: Spain 1-0 Argentina (AET): Ferran Torres' extra-time winner secures Spain's second title. Report as Ferran Torres scores the winning goal in extra time as Spain beat Argentina in the 2026 World Cup final; Lionel Messi is unable to win another world title on what is expected to be his final appearance at the tournament; Spain follow up Euro 2024 win with World Cup title. Spain won their second World Cup title after Ferran Torres' 106th-minute smashed finish earned a 1-0 win against defending champions Argentina in the 2026 final. Argentina did keep their shape well as Spain applied consistent pressure - especially after Chelsea's Enzo Fernandez was sent 