AM."},{"title":"Health experts say to mask up amid wildfire smoke - NBC News","url":"https://www.nbcnews.com/video/shorts/health-experts-say-to-mask-up-amid-wildfire-smoke-266885701771","description":"For an optimal experience visit our site on another browser. Health experts say to mask up amid wildfire smoke. Forest Service workers freed after being held hostage. Repairs begin for ruptured water break in Los Angeles. Trump calls for more election security as critics respond. California firefighters help pigeon struggling to breathe. Taylor Farms removes iceberg lettuce amid outbreak. Will Cape Verde see a post-World Cup tourism boost? Novak Djokovic's dance moves and GOATs. Uvalde residents describe damage from floods. 7.3-magnitude earthquake strikes off coast of southern Mexico. Blasts heard overnight in Qatar as U.S., Iran trade more strikes. Oscar-winning actor Brenda Fricker has died at 81. Craig Melvin addresses incident at TODAY's Studio 1A. Mamdani watches World Cup with Rikers Island inmates. Rescue efforts underway after massive landslide in China. Coast Guard rescues two people off the coast of Hawaii. Protests erupt in Ukraine over defense minister ousting. Iranian bridges damaged after sixth night of U.S. strikes."},{"title":"Zoox recalls self-driving cars because they may not detect smoke - SRN News","url":"https://srnnews.com/zoox-recalls-self-driving-cars-because-they-may-not-detect-smoke/","description":"Salem Radio Network News Friday, July 17, 2026. ## Business. WASHINGTON, July 17 (Reuters) – Amazon.com self-driving car unit Zoox said Friday it will recall 105 autonomous vehicles because they may not detect heavy smoke and could impede emergency personnel. Last week, the top U.S. auto safety official said self-driving car ​companies must quickly address a “clear pattern” of driverless vehicles interfering with ‌law enforcement and other first responders. Previous US equity funds suffer outflows as chip stocks slide. #### Salem News Channel | To