pain beats Argentina 1-0 to win World Cup 01:55 52m agoImage 24: Another American killed in war with Iran ### Another American killed in war with Iran 02:03 50m agoImage 25: Gas prices on the rise again ### Gas prices on the rise again 01:30 48m agoImage 26: Latest details on arrests of Tate brothers ### Latest details on arrests of Tate brothers 01:52 46m agoImage 27: The \"Super Scooper\" planes battling wildfires ### The \"Super Scooper\" planes battling wildfires 02:36 42m agoImage 28: What to know about Andy Burnham ### What to know about Andy Burnham 01:44 36m agoImage 29: The Hello Girls: America's first women soldiers ### The Hello Girls: America's first women soldiers 02:16 27m agoImage 30: The monarch butterfly migration mystery ### The monarch butterfly migration mystery 13:16 2h agoImage 31: Exonerees, survivors come together to heal ### Exonerees, survivors come together to heal 26:15 2h agoImage 32: Becker on election officials' arrest threats ### Becker on election officials' arrest threats 11:10 11h agoImage 33: Homan: \"Body cameras are the way to go\" ### Homan: \"Body cameras are the way to go\" 07:08 10h agoImage 34: Face the Nation: Hochul, Homan, Moynihan ### Face the Nation: Hochul, Homan, Moynihan 22:24 10h agoImage 35: Moynihan: \"Affordability is a challenge\" ### Moynihan: \"Affordability is a challenge\" 07:05 10h agoImage 36: Sen. Warner: Bases \"on and off under attack\" ### Sen. Warner: Bases \"on and off under attack\" 09:50 11h agoImage 37: Latest Trump nominees' confirmation hearings ### Latest Trump nominees' confirmation hearings 02:17 11h agoImage 38: Hochul: N.Y."},{"title":"‘T’ is for troops | Headlines - Defense News","url":"https://www.defensenews.com/video/2026/07/20/t-is-for-troops-headlines/","description":"### ‘T’ is for troops | Headlines. ###### The Pentagon rolls out a new program to screen troops for testosterone, and artillery shell makers struggle to keep up with rising demands in this week’s headlines. | Defense News Weekly Full Episode 7.21.26. ###### Is there a path forward for the Take Care of America’s Veterans Act? ###### New fitness standard takes hold across the Army | Defense News Weekly Full Episode 7.14.26. ###### Recruiting and retention at the forefront: a conversation with top enlisted leaders. ###### Pentagon turns to Mike Rowe to reenergize skilled trades training | Headlines. ###### The Medal of Honor and veteran transition assistance | Defense News Weekly Full Episode 7.7.26. ###### Pentagon grants Mike Rowe foundation $10 million for skilled trades program. ###### Russian troops survive just 20-30 minutes on Ukraine’s front lines, CIA director says. 5. ###### Canada to spend $1.4 billion on armored combat support vehicles built locally."}],"name":"web_search_tavily","tool_call_id":"toolu_017WRHCFrS7kqyEkdZ4rXPro"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"toolCalls":[{"id":"toolu_012UYD691gDLWwybcd8h8ent","name":"whatIAmDoing","arguments":{"message":"Found a big story cluster (US-Iran conflict). Digging deeper into specific headlines: Iran strikes, Ukraine protests, World Cup final, earthquake/landslide."}},{"id":"toolu_01BrjFfRBCPponmD2UWqCkqo","name":"web_search_tavily","arguments":{"query":"US Iran strikes today July 23 2026","count":6,"topic":"news"}},{"id":"toolu_01XVvLN6fDNtUgWZcjnP7oqk","name":"web_search_tavily","arguments":{"query":"Ukraine protests defense minister ousted July 2026","count":5,"topic":"news"}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"Delivered message to user.","name":"whatIAmDoing","tool_call_id":"toolu_012UYD691gDLWwybcd8h8ent"},{"role":"tool","content":[{"title":"Zelensky ousts popular defense minister, an architect of Ukraine’s drone program - The Washington Post","url":"https://www.washingtonpost.com/world/2026/07/16/zelensky-ousts-popular-defense-minister-an-architect-ukraines-drone-program/","description":"Mykhailo Fedorov's dismissal, part of a rebooting of the government announced Sunday, prompted protests in Kyiv. He was defense minister for barely six months. KYIV — Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky has ousted the country’s popular defense minister, Mykhailo Fedorov, prompting protests in Kyiv over a fear that his removal will jeopardize the war effort just as Ukraine is scoring victories on the front line. Although Zelensky did not announce it, Fedorov and members of the president’s Servant of the People party confirmed the dismissal late Wednesday — part of a rebooting of the government announced Sunday and among the latest signs of top-level turmoil. But he said that the decision was linked in part to his dispute with the head of the Ukrainian armed forces, Oleksandr Syrsky, with whom he disagreed over a number of issues related to the war."},{"title":"Zelensky sacks Ukraine’s military chief following widespread protests - CNN","url":"https://www.cnn.com/2026/07/21/europe/ukraine-military-chief-sacked-intl","description":"# Zelensky sacks Ukraine’s military chief following widespread protests. Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky has replaced Kyiv’s military chief, General Oleksandr Syrskyi, after days of widespread protests against the removal of the country’s popular defense minister, whose ousting revealed an unprecedented public split in the military over its strategy in the war against Russia. Mykhailo Drapatyi, who is the commander of Ukraine’s Joint Forces, will become Ukraine’s new commander-in-chief, Zelensky announced on Tuesday evening. Meanwhile, Zelensky offered Mykhailo Fedorov, whose removal as defense minister sparked this political storm, a “prominent position in government that would allow him to unify the technical component of our state and ensure its development.”. Aged 35 years old, Fedorov carved out a reputation as pioneering innovative approaches to technology and recruitment but clashed with other members of Ukraine’s defense establishment. His six-month tenure as defense minister coincided with Ukraine’s recent success on the battlefield and so his removal, amid disagreements with Syrskyi, caused a backlash against the military chief. *This is a developing story and will be updated.*."},{"title":"Ukrainians protest Zelensky’s ouster of his popular defense minister - Los Angeles Times","url":"https://www.latimes.com/world-nation/story/2026-07-16/ukrainians-protest-zelenskys-ouster-of-his-popular-defense-minister","description":"# Ukrainians protest Zelensky’s ouster of his popular defense minister. * Zelensky shakes up wartime leadership, firing popular 35-year-old defense minister Mykhailo Fedorov, a drone warfare innovator, sparking rare street protests as Russia’s invasion nears four-and-a-half years. KYIV, Ukraine — President Volodymyr Zelensky shook up his wartime government, drawing hundreds of Ukrainians into the streets Thursday to protest the ouster of his youthful defense minister — seen as an innovator of the country’s successful drone technology but who clashed with the traditional military establishment. The personnel overhaul, which included replacing his prime minister, could become a test of Zelensky’s political authority as Ukraine’s fight against Russia’s full-scale invasion approaches 4½ years. The moves threw Ukraine’s military leadership into an unwelcome crisis just as its actions against Russia were starting to bear fruit and came against a backdrop of Moscow’s unrelenting aerial attacks. Zelensky cited friction between outgoing Defense Minister Mykhailo Fedorov and Gen. Oleksandr Syrskyi, the commander of Ukraine’s armed forces."},{"title":"What to know about Ukraine's military shakeup - NPR","url":"https://www.npr.org/2026/07/22/g-s1-134813/ukraine-military-shakeup-zelenskyy","description":"**What to know about Ukraine's military shakeup** **After a week of nationwide protests over the direction of Ukraine's military strategy in the ongoing war with Russia, the Ukrainian military has a new commander, Mykhailo Drapatyi. # What to know about Ukraine's military shakeup. Protests erupted in Kyiv on Friday as President Volodymyr Zelenskyy dismissed Mykhailo Fedorov as Ukraine's defense minister. KYIV — After a week of nationwide protests over the direction of Ukraine's military strategy in the ongoing war with Russia, the Ukrainian military has a new armed forces commander, Mykhailo Drapatyi. In this photo provided by the Ukrainian Presidential Press Office, new commander-in-chief of Ukraine's Armed Forces Mykhailo Drapatyi looks on during his meeting with Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy in Kyiv, Ukraine, Monday, July 20, 2026. He is also the face of a younger, post-Soviet generation of military leaders in Ukraine who are adapting more quickly to a tech-focused approach to the battlefield."},{"title":"Protests continue in Ukraine over defense minister's firing - NPR","url":"https://www.npr.org/2026/07/20/nx-s1-5899777/protests-continue-in-ukraine-over-defense-ministers-firing","description":"* Keyboard shortcuts for audio player. **Protests continue in Ukraine over defense minister's firing** **Protests over President Volodymyr Zelenskyy's dismissal of the country's defense minister coincide with a fresh wave of Russian strikes across Ukraine.**. ### Europe. # Protests continue in Ukraine over defense minister's firing. * **`<iframe src=\"https://www.npr.org/player/embed/nx-s1-5899777/nx-s1-9854967\" width=\"100%\" height=\"290\" frameborder=\"0\" scrolling=\"no\" title=\"NPR embedded audio player\">`**. Protests over President Volodymyr Zelenskyy's dismissal of the country's defense minister coincide with a fresh wave of Russian strikes across Ukraine."}],"name":"web_search_tavily","tool_call_id":"toolu_01XVvLN6fDNtUgWZcjnP7oqk"},{"role":"tool","content":[{"title":"U.S. and Iranian attacks continue as tensions mount on a key waterway in the Red Sea - Jefferson Public Radio","url":"https://www.ijpr.org/npr-news/2026-07-22/u-s-and-iranian-attacks-continue-as-tensions-mount-on-a-key-waterway-in-the-red-sea","description":"# U.S. and Iranian attacks continue as tensions mount on a key waterway in the Red Sea. Published July 22, 2026 at 3:46 AM PDT. The U.S. military launched more airstrikes on Iran early Wednesday as Iran hit back against U.S. military targets in the Gulf and Jordan. It said the attacks were aimed at degrading Iran's control over the Strait of Hormuz – a vital shipping channel. The Shia Muslim Houthis are backed by Iran and a key part of Iran's \"axis of resistance,\" which has joined in attacks on U.S. and Israeli targets. Iran said Wednesday it again targeted an air base in eastern Jordan where three U.S. military personnel were killed in an attack last week. Iran blames the U.S. for the missile strike on the first day of the U.S.-Israeli war on Iran and says it killed at least 156 people, including 120 children. Iran says 168 students and teachers were killed in a U.S. missile strike on the school in southern Iran on Feb. 28."},{"title":"U.S. and Iranian attacks continue as tensions mount on a key waterway in the Red Sea - Northern Public Radio","url":"https://www.northernpublicradio.org/2026-07-22/u-s-and-iranian-attacks-continue-as-tensions-mount-on-a-key-waterway-in-the-red-sea","description":"# U.S. and Iranian attacks continue as tensions mount on a key waterway in the Red Sea. Published July 22, 2026 at 5:46 AM CDT. The U.S. military launched more airstrikes on Iran early Wednesday as Iran hit back against U.S. military targets in the Gulf and Jordan. It said the attacks were aimed at degrading Iran's control over the Strait of Hormuz – a vital shipping channel. Iranian state media reported explosions in seven Iranian provinces and said attacks included a strike on an electrical installation close to a nuclear power plant in Bushehr province. The Shia Muslim Houthis are backed by Iran and a key part of Iran's \"axis of resistance,\" which has joined in attacks on U.S. and Israeli targets. Iran said Wednesday it again targeted an air base in eastern Jordan where three U.S. military personnel were killed in an attack last week."},{"title":"US launches strikes against Iran for ninth consecutive night, sirens sound in Kuwait, Bahrain - The Jerusalem Post","url":"https://www.jpost.com/middle-east/iran-news/article-903012","description":"# US launches strikes against Iran for ninth consecutive night, sirens sound in Kuwait, Bahrain. ## \"The strikes will continue degrading Iranian military capabilities used to attack commercial vessels and civilian mariners transiting the Strait of Hormuz,\" CENTCOM wrote. A munition is launched from a U.S. warship at an unknown location, during what U.S. Central Command (CENTCOM) says are strikes on Iran, in this screen grab taken from a handout video released on July 18, 2026. (photo credit: US CENTRAL COMMAND/HANDOUT VIA REUTERS). The United States launched a new wave of strikes against Iran early Monday morning, US Central Command (CENTCOM) stated in a post to X/Twitter. This marks the ninth consecutive night of US strikes against Iran. Iran has been retaliating by targeting US bases and other infrastructure in neighboring countries. Earlier on Sunday night, the Kuwait military announced it was intercepting multiple hostile drones. Additionally, sirens were sounded in Kuwait. *This is a developing story.*."},{"title":"US military says it completed latest strikes on Iran, marking 6th consecutive night of attacks - Reuters","url":"https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/us-military-says-it-completed-latest-strikes-iran-marking-6th-consecutive-night-2026-07-17/","description":"## Browse World. Smoke rises from an explosion at an unknown location, during what U.S. Central Command (CENTCOM) says are strikes on Iran, in this screen grab taken from a handout video released on July 15, 2026. U.S. Central Command/Handout via REUTERS Purchase Licensing Rights, opens new tab. WASHINGTON, July 16 (Reuters) - The U.S. military said late on Thursday it completed its latest wave of strikes on Iran that were carried out at ​President Donald Trump's direction and marked a sixth consecutive night of American strikes. The Reuters Iran Briefing newsletter keeps you informed with the latest developments and analysis of the Iran war. *   Iranian news outlets also reported U.S. strikes late on ​Thursday on three bridges and the train station in coastal Bandar Khamir and a U.S. missile attack on Iranshahr Airport in southeastern Iran. *   The Iran war began when the U.S. and Israel attacked Iran on February 28 and Iran responded with its own strikes on Israel and Gulf states that ⁠host ​U.S. bases. *   About Reuters, opens new tab."},{"title":"Iran claims US warplanes strike in southern Iran - The Jerusalem Post","url":"https://www.jpost.com/middle-east/iran-news/article-902943","description":"# US warplanes strike in southern Iran, CENTCOM wraps up eighth round of strikes - report. ## This comes after CENTCOM said that it had completed its eighth consecutive night of strikes against Iran overnight on Saturday. Smoke rises from an explosion at an unknown location, during what U.S. Central Command (CENTCOM) says are strikes on Iran, in this screen grab taken from a handout video released on July 18, 2026. (photo credit: U.S. Central Command/Handout via REUTERS). US warplanes reportedly struck near the city of Shadagan in southern Iran on Sunday, state TV reported. Earlier on Sunday, US Central Command (CENTCOM) said that it had completed its eighth consecutive night of strikes against Iran and hit Iranian military coastal surveillance and air defense facilities. It also targeted the Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps forces that launched attacks against US service members in Jordan on July 17. *This is a developing story.*."},{"title":"US strikes Iran for 9th night, confirms American servicemember killed in Iraq - The Times of Israel","url":"https://www.timesofisrael.com/us-strikes-iran-for-9th-night-confirms-american-servicemember-killed-in-iraq/","description":"## Explosions reported in several Iranian cities as IRGC claims it hit oil tankers trying to cross Hormuz, struck assets in Kuwait; Iran said to suspect US planning ground operation. Video footage shared by US Central Command on July 19, 2026, shows forces launching a ninth consecutive evening of strikes against Iran. US forces struck Iran for a ninth consecutive day on Monday as the number of confirmed American military deaths in the renewed fighting rose to three, and concerns grew over shipping through the Strait of Hormuz, which the Trump administration accused the Islamic Republic of seeking to control “as leverage against the world.”. Announcing the latest casualties in the war, the US military said on Sunday that a servicemember was killed on Saturday in northern Iraq, where the US has military bases, “during a controlled detonation” of a downed Iranian attack drone."}],"name":"web_search_tavily","tool_call_id":"toolu_01BrjFfRBCPponmD2UWqCkqo"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"toolCalls":[{"id":"toolu_01NuaiQesaMohhT2BqL8XNpu","name":"whatIAmDoing","arguments":{"message":"Checking World Cup final result, China landslide, and any other major stories from today."}},{"id":"toolu_01M5LvsFKE5ZZ32YNJtURMBC","name":"web_search_tavily","arguments":{"query":"Spain wins World Cup Argentina final 2026","count":5,"topic":"news"}},{"id":"toolu_0181zTz6i4pxSfDLLod2RfiW","name":"web_search_tavily","arguments":{"query":"China landslide rescue July 2026","count":5,"topic":"news"}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"Delivered message to user.","name":"whatIAmDoing","tool_call_id":"toolu_01NuaiQesaMohhT2BqL8XNpu"},{"role":"tool","content":[{"title":"Rescuers race to find survivors in the rain after a landslide in China kills at least 8 - The Washington Post","url":"https://www.washingtonpost.com/world/2026/07/18/china-landslide-chonqing-rain/00c48b78-8267-11f1-8a16-393bd03340b0_story.html","description":"# Rescuers race to find survivors in the rain after a landslide in China kills at least 8. Rescue crews are racing against the clock to find survivors after a landslide in the southwestern Chinese city of Chongqing killed at least eight people and left 34 missing. Rescuers stand by along the bridge as they prepare to conduct a search and rescue operation at the scene of a landslide in Pengshui County in southwestern China’s Chongqing on Saturday, July 18, 2026. CHONGQING, China — Rescue crews on Saturday raced to find survivors from a landslide in the southwestern Chinese city of Chongqing that killed at least eight people and left 34 missing. The landslide occurred in Pengshui County on Friday morning on the outskirts of Chongqing municipality, when massive amounts of rocks and soil washed down a slope, burying more than 10 residential buildings, state broadcaster CCTV said."},{"title":"China landslide kills at least 8 as rescuers race to find survivors in the rain - New York Post","url":"https://nypost.com/2026/07/18/world-news/china-landslide-kills-at-least-8-as-rescuers-race-to-find-survivors-in-the-rain/","description":"# China landslide kills at least 8 as rescuers race to find survivors in rain. Rescue crews on Saturday raced to find survivors from a landslide in the southwestern Chinese city of Chongqing that killed at least eight people and left 34 missing. The landslide occurred in Pengshui County on Friday morning on the outskirts of Chongqing municipality, when massive amounts of rocks and soil washed down a slope, burying more than 10 residential buildings, state broadcaster CCTV said. CCTV said persistent rain hit Pengshui from Friday night to Saturday morning and nearly 8 inches of rainfall was recorded at a weather station. As the rain eased slightly, rescue teams entered the site to conduct on-the-ground inspections of the collapsed buildings and riverbank areas. Once the search of the surrounding areas is complete, officers will drill into the boulders and fill the holes with explosives to break them apart, it said."},{"title":"Rescuers in China search the rubble for survivors of landslide that killed 8 and left 34 missing - AP News","url":"https://apnews.com/article/china-landslide-chongqing-deadly-bd443c1fc952b1cc073cd03f054dc9ff","description":"Test Your News I.Q. 2026 Elections Election Results Election calendar White House Congress Supreme Court The latest AP-NORC polls. Your home base for in-depth reporting from the world of sports. Founded in 1846, AP today remains the most trusted source of fast, accurate, unbiased news in all formats and the essential provider of the technology and services vital to the news business. Rescuers work at the site of a landslide in Pengshui County in southwestern China’s Chongqing on Sunday, July 19, 2026. Rescuers use heavy machinery to clear rubble to search for trapped persons on the site of a landslide in Pengshui County, southwestern China’s Chongqing on Sunday, July 19, 2026. Residents watch as rescuers work at the site of a landslide in Pengshui County in southwestern China’s Chongqing on Sunday, July 19, 2026. CHONGQING, China (AP) — Rescue crews used excavators on Sunday to comb through the rubble in search of survivors from a landslide in the southwestern Chinese city of Chongqing that killed at least eight people and left another 34 missing."},{"title":"Landslide kills eight in southwest China's Chongqing, 34 still missing - Reuters","url":"https://www.reuters.com/business/environment/landslide-buries-residents-southwest-chinas-chongqing-2026-07-17/","description":"Exclusive news, data and analytics for financial market professionals Learn more about Refinitiv. ## Browse World. ## Browse Business. Image 2: Rescue workers search for survivors at the site of a landslide in Chongqing. Item 1 of 5 Rescue workers search for survivors at the site of a landslide along Wujiang river in Pengshui Miao and Tujia Autonomous County, Chongqing, China July 17, 2026. **[1/5]**Rescue workers search for survivors at the site of a landslide along Wujiang river in Pengshui Miao and Tujia Autonomous County, Chongqing, China July 17, 2026. BEIJING, July 17 (Reuters) - Eight people were killed ​and 34 others are still missing after a landslide in a ‌county in the southwestern Chinese city of Chongqing on Friday, local government officials told a press conference. In a late Friday directive, President Xi Jinping ordered search and ​rescue operations to be carried out for the missing and called ​for an investigation into the cause of the landslide. *   About Reuters, opens new tab. *   Media Center, opens new tab."},{"title":"Landslide in southwest China traps people, rescue efforts underway - AP News","url":"https://apnews.com/article/china-landslide-chongqing-buildings-127e504babcf9d70773e4ec67af34952","description":"Test Your News I.Q. 2026 Elections Election Results Election calendar White House Congress Supreme Court The latest AP-NORC polls. 2026 Elections Election Results Election calendar White House Congress Supreme Court The latest AP-NORC polls. Founded in 1846, AP today remains the most trusted source of fast, accurate, unbiased news in all formats and the essential provider of the technology and services vital to the news business. In this photo released by Xinhua News Agency, rescuers conduct search and rescue operation on the site of the landslide in Pengshui County in southwestern China’s Chongqing on Friday, July 17, 2026. In this photo taken and provided by Mimama, smoke rise as resident buildings toppled by rocks and muds following a landslide in Pengshui County in southwestern China’s Chongqing on Friday, July 17, 2026. This photo taken and provided by Mimama shows firefighters arrive to the landslide scene in Pengshui County in southwestern China’s Chongqing on Friday, July 17, 2026."}],"name":"web_search_tavily","tool_call_id":"toolu_0181zTz6i4pxSfDLLod2RfiW"},{"role":"tool","content":[{"title":"Spain, scoring late, tops Argentina, 1-0, to win 2026 World Cup - The Washington Post","url":"https://www.washingtonpost.com/sports/2026/07/19/spain-scoring-late-tops-argentina-1-0-win-2026-world-cup/","description":"# Spain, scoring late, tops Argentina, 1-0, to win 2026 World Cup. A tournament that began as a grand experiment across three countries ended with a finish worthy of all its sprawl: Spain beating Argentina, 1-0, in extra time. Ferran Torres, Spain’s flashy 26-year-old forward, put the ball high into the net in the 106th minute of Sunday’s World Cup final, breaking a scoreless tie and sending all of Spain into delirium. And with that, a tournament that began as a grand experiment across three countries ended with a finish worthy of all its sprawl: Spain beating Argentina, 1*-*0, in extra time to win its first World Cup title since 2010 and deny Lionel Messi one more implausible addition to his legend. To get here, Spain masterfully navigated the biggest, most complicated World Cup the sport has seen, bouncing across a continent, slaying the game’s giants and adding both theatrics and closure to a tournament that was never short on drama."},{"title":"2026 World Cup: Spain 1-0 Argentina (AET): Ferran Torres' extra-time winner secures Spain's second title - Sky Sports","url":"https://www.skysports.com/football/news/12098/13564318/2026-world-cup-spain-1-0-argentina-aet-ferran-torres-extra-time-winner-secures-spains-second-title","description":"# 2026 World Cup: Spain 1-0 Argentina (AET): Ferran Torres' extra-time winner secures Spain's second title. Report as Ferran Torres scores the winning goal in extra time as Spain beat Argentina in the 2026 World Cup final; Lionel Messi is unable to win another world title on what is expected to be his final appearance at the tournament; Spain follow up Euro 2024 win with World Cup title. Spain won their second World Cup title after Ferran Torres' 106th-minute smashed finish earned a 1-0 win against defending champions Argentina in the 2026 final. Argentina did keep their shape well as Spain applied consistent pressure - especially after Chelsea's Enzo Fernandez was sent off for a reckless second yellow at the end of normal time - and relied on Martinez to make a string of saves. But there was no fairytale end to Messi's expected final World Cup appearance, with the Argentina skipper anonymous for much of the game."},{"title":"World Cup brawl sees Argentina player putting hand on throat of Spain opponent after match - Fox News","url":"https://www.foxnews.com/sports/world-cup-brawl-argentina-player-putting-hand-throat-spain-opponent-after-match","description":"* #### Every Teenager To Start In A World Cup Final — And Win It. * #### FIFA World Cup: Every Winner Since 1930, From Uruguay To Spain In 2026. * #### How to Watch the 2026 FIFA World Cup: Scores for Every Match. * #### Spain beats Argentina to win 2026 FIFA World Cup behind Ferran Torres' extra-time goal. * #### Spain wins the 2026 FIFA World Cup in extra-time. * #### Spain wins the 2026 FIFA World Cup. #### Spain wins the 2026 FIFA World Cup. Fox News chief correspondent Jonathan Hunt reports on Spain winning the 2026 FIFA World Cup final against Argentina in a match at New York New Jersey Stadium on ‘The Big Weekend Show.’. Spain’s exciting FIFA World Cup victory over Argentina in extra time was marred by a post-match brawl that included Leandro Paredes and Eric García. Leandro Paredes of Argentina confronts Eric Garcia of Spain after the FIFA World Cup 2026 final match at New York New Jersey Stadium in East Rutherford, N.J., on July 19, 2026."},{"title":"Spain beats Argentina to win 2026 FIFA World Cup behind Ferran Torres' extra-time goal - Fox News","url":"https://www.foxnews.com/sports/spain-beats-argentina-win-2026-fifa-world-cup-behind-ferran-torres-extra-time-goal","description":"* #### 2026 World Cup Title Odds: Spain Favored Over Argentina In Final. * #### 2026 World Cup Young Player of the Tournament Odds: Lamine Yamal Favored. * #### How to watch Argentina vs Spain: Live stream the 2026 FIFA World Cup final match. * #### Argentina, Spain cap off 2026 FIFA World C