{"format_version":1,"trace_id":"JCdVnnRn7lhXe8HDoU0pv","project_id":"agency-lang","span_id":"ZuTzruHYGCWZ","parent_span_id":"hS4HZGU_m5f1","data":{"type":"toolCall","toolName":"researchAgent","args":{"userMsg":"What are the top news stories today, July 23, 2026? Please give a brief summary of the 5-6 most significant world/national news headlines from today.","agencyTopic":false},"output":"## Top News — July 23, 2026\n\n**US-Iran War Escalates, New Front Opens in Red Sea**\n\nThe conflict has reached its 12th consecutive night of US strikes, with Iranian media reporting explosions in the cities of Bushehr, Ahvaz and Sirik. Iran's Foreign Minister Abbas Araghchi said Tehran's defence doctrine is an \"eye for an eye,\" after Trump warned US forces would bomb an Iranian bridge or power plant every time Iranian forces hit a ship in the Strait of Hormuz. The US has also deployed heavier firepower — the US military used a B-1 long-range bomber on Tuesday to strike Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps targets in Iran, the first such mission since fighting resumed 12 days ago. Meanwhile, Iran-backed Houthi militants said they struck two tankers in the Red Sea, risking a new chokepoint that could further disrupt global energy supplies and spike prices. The human toll continues to climb: a total of 18 US service members have died in the war, and about 550 have been wounded so far, while at least 1,700 Iranian civilians have been killed.\n\n**Ukraine's Military Shakeup Concludes After Week of Protests**\n\nAfter a week of nationwide protests over the direction of Ukraine's military strategy, the Ukrainian military has a new commander, Mykhailo Drapatyi, replacing Gen. Oleksandr Syrsky following the controversial firing of popular defense minister Mykhailo Fedorov. The new chief is not backing down from the fight — Drapatyi said the military would \"continue and intensify offensive operations in all domains\" as Kyiv seeks to pressure Russian forces, while Russia claimed fresh strikes on Odesa port facilities and drone warehouses.\n\n**World Cup Final Ends in Drama and Controversy**\n\nSpain beat Argentina 1-0 in extra time to win its first World Cup title since 2010, with Ferran Torres scoring in the 106th minute, denying Lionel Messi one more shot at glory. The match wasn't without controversy — a post-match brawl broke out involving Argentina's Leandro Paredes and Spain's Eric García, prompting FIFA to launch an investigation.\n\n**Trump's Election-Fraud Claims Draw Scrutiny**\n\nPresident Trump has renewed his push on election integrity: in a primetime address, Trump said the People's Republic of China carried out what is believed to be the largest compromise of election data in history, resulting in China's acquisition of 220 million US voter files, and touted a DHS report claiming roughly 278,000 noncitizens are registered to vote in federal elections. However, newly declassified documents cited by the administration to back these claims offer scant evidence, and don't fully support Trump's allegations. Separately, Secretary of State Marco Rubio struck a cordial tone with China's top diplomat despite Trump's meddling claims, in an apparent bid to ease relations ahead of Xi Jinping's expected US visit in September.\n\n**China Landslide Recovery Continues in Chongqing**\n\nRescue operations remain underway after a landslide in southwestern China's Chongqing killed at least eight people and left 34 missing, after massive amounts of rock and soil buried more than 10 residential buildings in Pengshui County amid heavy rain.\n\n**Domestic Notes: ICE Vetting Concerns & Wisconsin Police Shooting**\n\nRecent fatal shootings by ICE officers in Texas and Maine have raised questions from police experts about vetting, as the agency has hired more than 12,000 officers in less than a year amid its rapid hiring push. Separately, a Madison, Wisconsin police officer shot and killed a man who had injured him with a knife while resisting arrest near the state Capitol.\n\n---\n*Sources: NYT, NBC News, Al Jazeera, CBS News, Axios, Washington Post, AP, CNN.*","model":"\"claude-sonnet-5\"","timeTaken":183525.793083,"threadId":"2","timestamp":"2026-07-23T13:58:13.443Z"}}
