ckage path (e.g. `git log <range> -- packages/agency-lang/`) so you report changes relevant to THIS package, not the whole repo. Note in the report if you scoped it.\",\"Report the changelog's existing conventions precisely (heading style, version/date format, section groupings like Added/Fixed/Changed, bullet tone and typical length) so the user can match the pattern — this is item 1 and easy to under-deliver on.\",\"Deliver a report only. Present all four requested items clearly and separately; give enough per-commit detail that the user can write 1–2 sentence bullets themselves.\"],\"checklist\":[\"Report includes the FULL current contents of changelog.md (item 1) — verify by confirming the file was actually read from the agency-lang package directory, not summarized or truncated.\",\"Report explicitly describes the changelog format/pattern: heading style, version+date format, section groupings, and typical bullet tone/length — verify each of these attributes is named.\",\"Report states the current version string exactly as it appears in package.json's `version` field — verify by reading package.json (in the correct package dir).\",\"Report documents whether version git tags exist and which pattern matched — verify that `git tag` was run with at least one pattern (plain, `v`-prefixed, and package-scoped) before any 'no tags' conclusion.\",\"Report lists the commits since the last release, produced from an explicit range (e.g. `git log <tag-or-commit>..HEAD`), and states how the starting point was determined (tag vs. last-changelog-entry fallback).\",\"Report groups changes by theme (features / fixes / docs / internal) with substance-level detail — verify that at least one commit's actual diff was inspected via `git log --stat`, `git show`, or `git diff`, not just subject lines.\",\"NO files were edited — verify no write/edit tool was used and no `git commit`/file-modifying command was run; the deliverable is a report only.\",\"Git history was scoped appropriately