kill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>Attachments</name>\n    <description>Explains how to send images and files to the model in an LLM call, using the `image()` and `file()` builders from `std::thread`.</description>\n    <location>attachments.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>Basic syntax</name>\n    <description>Overview of Agency&apos;s TypeScript-derived syntax, covering primitive types, variables, arrays, objects, functions, and other core language constructs.</description>\n    <location>basic-syntax.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>Blocks</name>\n    <description>Explains Agency&apos;s block syntax, used in place of lambdas for higher-order functions like `map`, including custom block-taking functions and inline block syntax.</description>\n    <location>blocks.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>Build Integration</name>\n    <description>How to compile Agency code as part of a JavaScript build (Vite, etc.) and call it from the backend of a web app.</description>\n    <location>build-integration.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>Built-in Functions</name>\n    <description>Reference table of every user-facing built-in function and language construct available in any `.agency` file without an import, covering LLM calls, checkpointing, interrupts, concurrency, and more.</description>\n    <location>builtins.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>Callbacks</name>\n    <description>Documents Agency&apos;s callback hooks (e.g. `onNodeStart`) that can be registered from Agency files via `callback(...)` or passed in from TypeScript when invoking a node, including scoping rules and the no-interrupts-in-callbacks restriction.</description>\n    <location>callbacks.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>Checkpointing</name>\n    <description>Explains Agency&apos;s ability to snapshot and restore execution state via `checkpoint`, `getCheckpoint`, and `restore`, which underpins interrupts, error recovery, forks, and the time-travel debugger.</description>\n    <location>checkpointing.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>Common functions</name>\n    <description>How to use common functions in Agency, such as printing, getting user input, and reading/writing files.</description>\n    <location>common-functions.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>Compiling and Running Code</name>\n    <description>How to run Agency programs and compile them to JavaScript, including watch mode and the classic global-install gotcha.</description>\n    <location>compiling-and-running.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>List comprehensions</name>\n    <description>Build a new list from an existing one in a single expression, either sequentially or concurrently.</description>\n    <location>comprehensions.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>Concurrency</name>\n    <description>Covers Agency&apos;s concurrency primitives including `parallel`, `seq`, `fork`, and `race` for running multiple branches of work simultaneously.</description>\n    <location>concurrency.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>Cross-thread context sharing</name>\n    <description>How to inspect, read, and resume other `thread {}` blocks in the same run using `listThreads()`, `getThread()`, and the named arguments on `thread {}`. Includes a categorize-and-route example.</description>\n    <location>cross-thread-context.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>Custom Providers</name>\n    <description>How to create and use custom model providers in Agency.</description>\n    <location>custom-providers.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>Debugging</name>\n    <description>A walkthrough of Agency&apos;s interactive terminal debugger — stepping forward, rewinding through checkpoints, overriding variables, and inspecting panels.</description>\n    <location>debugging.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>Developer Tools</name>\n    <description>