fects in interrupts, allowing handlers to respond differently based on the effect.</description>\n    <location>effects.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>Error handling</name>\n    <description>Describes Agency&apos;s exception-free approach to errors using the `Result` type, with `success`/`failure` constructors and patterns for unwrapping results.</description>\n    <location>error-handling.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>Exercise 1</name>\n    <description>Practice exercises for getting familiar with Agency&apos;s syntax and features.</description>\n    <location>exercise-1.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>Functions</name>\n    <description>Covers function declarations in Agency, including docstrings (used as LLM tool descriptions), default and variadic arguments, named parameters, and block syntax.</description>\n    <location>functions.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>Getting Started</name>\n    <description>Introduction to the Agency language guide, covering installation, a quick &quot;hello world&quot; example, and how to navigate the rest of the documentation.</description>\n    <location>getting-started.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>Global variable initialization</name>\n    <description>How Agency initializes top-level values that reference other top-level values from different modules.</description>\n    <location>global-var-initialization.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>Global vs Static Variables</name>\n    <description>Per-run isolation of global variables vs static variables that initialize once and persist across runs.</description>\n    <location>global-vs-static.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>Guards</name>\n    <description>Documents the `guard` function for capping the cost and/or compute time of a block of work, returning a `Result` that lets you handle budget overruns.</description>\n    <location>guards.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <sk